---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config/site';
const updated = 'October 2026';
---
<BaseLayout title="Privacy" description="How Tenorworth handles information collected through this website." noindex={false}>
  <article class="container-prose py-20 sm:py-28">
    <p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p>
    <h1 class="mt-6 text-4xl sm:text-5xl">Privacy policy</h1>
    <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-ink-muted">Last updated {updated}</p>

    <div class="mt-10 space-y-8 leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl text-ink">Who we are</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">{SITE.name} is a practice brand of {SITE.legalEntity}. This policy covers information collected through {SITE.url}.</p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl text-ink">What we collect</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">If you email us or book a call, we keep your name, contact details, and what you tell us about your business so that we can respond. We use analytics to understand how the site is used.</p>
        <p class="mt-3">We also use the LinkedIn Insight Tag. It sets cookies and tells LinkedIn which pages of this site a browser has visited, so that we can measure our LinkedIn advertising and show our posts to people who have been here. LinkedIn gives us aggregate reports only. It does not tell us who individual visitors are.</p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl text-ink">How we use it</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">To reply to you, to prepare for a conversation you have requested, to improve this site, and to measure our advertising. We do not sell or rent personal information, and we do not use the details you send us for advertising.</p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl text-ink">Client data</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">Data shared during an engagement is governed by the engagement agreement and any business associate, confidentiality, or data processing terms it includes, not by this policy.</p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl text-ink">Your choices</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">You can ask us to correct or delete what we hold about you at any time by writing to <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`} class="link-quiet text-ink">{SITE.email}</a>.</p>
        <p class="mt-3">The LinkedIn tag does not load when your browser sends a Global Privacy Control signal. You can also turn off this kind of advertising in your LinkedIn ad settings.</p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
